21.14 Resource limits

Centralized hard limits cover:
- total input bytes;
- decompressed bytes;
- IR step count;
- selector depth;
- parsed structure depth;
- collection size;
- regex pattern size;
- regex input size;
- worker execution duration;
- archive expansion where applicable.

The implementation selects explicit constants, centralizes them, documents them, and regression-tests every boundary.
Limits must not be scattered throughout the code.

BASE_SOURCE-L1953-1966.text:
22.2 test-worker.js

Test execution occurs in a Web Worker.

The worker:
- receives only normalized Test IR;
- receives only explicitly bound artifact bytes;
- receives only immutable permitted metadata;
- has no arbitrary network access;
- has no unrestricted project access;
- enforces resource limits;
- returns a deterministic normalized result;
- can be terminated on timeout;
- cannot block the UI thread.

